  "worked_solution": "Since we need to multiply by $\\frac{1}{2}$, we split the whole into $2$ equal parts horizontally and ensure that $1$ of the parts remains shaded.\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14130839/assets/2f06814dd3cbc6990fad45eb05bc77856f0eda54185388d2c1e2795275beadad.png)\n\nFrom the picture on the right, we obtain that the shaded part represents $\\frac{3}{10}$ of the whole.\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\frac{3}{5}\\times \\frac{1}{2}=\\frac{3}{10}.\n$$",
